// Each rule below is one way the JSON `rule` can match.
// Columns after `at` are the metavariables the JSON's message, anchor or `each` names: one finding per distinct row.
.violation PT011(at: node, x: node) "Add `match=` with the expected message (or `check=` on pytest 8.4+) to `pytest.raises({x})`, or expect a more specific exception, so unrelated `{x}` errors do not pass."
    suppress noqa "PT011"
PT011(X, n) :- pt011_exc(n, X), pt011_exc_slot(n).
PT011(X, n) :- pt011_ann_string(n, X).

